575 0 obj
<<
/Title (This study reproduced the machine learning methodology of Paper 3 and extended the evaluation with an empirical investigation of duplicate observations and train-test contamination.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 408 0 R
/Next 719 0 R
>>
endobj
576 0 obj
<<
/Title (Overall, the findings demonstrate that exceptionally high medical machine learning performance should be interpreted cautiously when duplicate observations are present. Rigorous duplicate auditing, appropriate partitioning strategies, and independent validation are essential for obtaining more reliable estimates of model generalisation and clinical usefulness.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 408 0 R
/Prev 720 0 R
>>
endobj
